  "original_source_text": "Cache partitioning mechanisms improve system performance by judiciously adjusting cache space among applications. Its effectiveness can be enhanced by partitioning in both time and space. However, existing solutions are limited to only one dimension. This paper presents Cachence, a fine-grained cache partitioning mechanism in both time and space. Cachence profiles cache access patterns with theoretically guaranteed accuracy while incurring fixed storage overhead. Based on runtime microarchitectural statistics, we also propose a lightweight yet precise performance prediction model. Our evaluation shows that Cachence outperforms existing approaches by an average of 9.5% to 28.2%, and up to 48.8% on a 16-core system.",
